  "$id": "https://tego.dev/spec/record/v1/live-fields.schema.json",
  "title": "Run record v1: the live changes' fields (21 to 41)",
  "description": "One document per line, as mvp-fields.schema.json has it: the line's kind, the revision of its ledger (its run_start's record_minor) and its payload (a refused line also its rule). The schema describes a gap's live_block (a person's live block, a time limit's end, an Adjustable run's fence entry lifted, restored or refused) and live_control (a pause or a resume), run_start's live_mode and live_fence, the rules a refused line carries under live.fence[...], live.lift[...] and live.block[read:...], live.block[write:...], and the revision below which each is refused. A field the ledger writer moved to a blob (live_block_blob, live_control_blob) stands for the field. A member the schema does not name is ignored, as a reader of a later revision's line ignores it. pkg/spec/record (Event.ValidateAt) also refuses what JSON Schema cannot say: a key spelt with another letter case, a null anywhere in a field, a rule that is not live.block[<kind>:<value>] (or live.fence[...], live.lift[...]) of the change's own kind and value, a value of more than 4096 bytes (maxLength counts characters), a note of more than 200 bytes, or of text that is not printable (the schema holds the printable classes and 200 characters) [live-block], addrs that are not canonical, unmapped, sorted addresses with no repeat, a full list where addrs_more is above 0 [live-block] (the schema holds only that addrs_more above 0 needs a list of 32), a fence entry whose rule is not live.fence[<kind>:<value>] of its own, a fence listing a rule twice, and a repeated key, which is no I-JSON and is refused before the schema. spec/record/v1/fixtures/live holds the documents, and internal/testutil/jsonschema's TestRecordLiveFixturesAgainstSchema runs them through the real validator.",
